WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.533
We begin

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.067
with an

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.801
urgent search

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.869
and rescue operation

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:03.970
that is currently underway

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.372
in the Atlantic Ocean.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.406
Right now, U.S.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.340
Coast Guard officials

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.542
are racing to find a submersible

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.012
operated by a company that runs tours

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.847
of the Titanic wreckage.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.482
Officials say that this was reported

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.117
overdue on Sunday

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.119
and is said to have only 96 hours

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.453
of survival time.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.255
We are told several government

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.890
agencies and deep companies

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.925
are working on reestablishing contact

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.794
with this submersible.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.461
CNN's Miguel

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.763
Marquez is joining us

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.997
now live with more details

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:31.898
on this Miguel.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.234
What do you know at this point?

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:34.868
You know, the company

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.504
that runs this operation, Ocean

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.073
Gate Expeditions, does everything from,

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.143
you know, science underwater

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.278
to photography and video

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.213
to tourism as well,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.549
to places like the Titanic wreckage

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.084
and have done it for quite some time.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.053
It costs about $250,000

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.721
per person to do this.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.722
What we don't know

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.957
is exactly who was on this submersible.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:58.725
It can hold

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.093
if it is the one

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.062
that they have up on their website,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.330
it can hold up to five people.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.733
It has 96 hours worth of air.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.967
But it all depends on

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.303
how many people are on that submersible

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.704
and how deep it is.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.206
We know that the U.S.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.608
Coast Guard, along with Canadian

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.678
Air Force as well, is assisting in this.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.713
They're all moving to this area

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.515
by fixed wing and boats

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.150
trying to get to the area

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.251
so that they can help out.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.353
But look, this is extremely remote.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.389
These depths are incredibly deep.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.492
The Titanic itself is about 3800 meter.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.793
That's about 13,000

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.861
feet under the under

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:35.595
the ocean,

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.098
just extreme, extreme, remote

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.899
and difficult place

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.702
to operate on a good day.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.438
The Canadians do have a P-8

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.706
or a Poseidon aircraft

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.241
that does have some ability

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.742
to see basically underwater

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.444
as a sub hunting

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.145
aircraft

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.747
that can see underwater to some degree.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.883
But it's not clear

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.686
if they know where this this craft is

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:03.056
and and what exactly happened to it.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.457
As you mentioned,

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.426
they have about 96 hours of air

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.495
in sort of a perfect conditions,

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.496
but it's not clear

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.531
given that this was reported

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.700
missing 24 hours ago now,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.568
how much more air they might have

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.403
and where this search goes from now.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:17.837
Right now

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.705
all hands on deck

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.174
trying to find this craft Brianna.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.575
All right, Miguel,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.477
thank you for the very latest there.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.912
I want to turn now to an expert on this.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.381
We have Butch Hendrick here with us.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:28.748
Butch,

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.351
you have 30 years of experience

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.886
as a rescue diver.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:33.853
You're also the president

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.321
and founder of Lifeguard Systems,

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.856
which is an international rescue

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.125
and recovery training company.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.162
Do you know where you begin

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:45.265
with a rescue like this?

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:48.701
Well, I think the same

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.969
way the United States

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:50.670
Coast Guard

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.772
and the Canadians will be working.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.742
The first thing is to discover, does

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.846
the unit submersible have releasable

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.415
beacons, emergency beacons?

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.050
So if it does, then

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.417
it would have

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.085
possibly released a beacon

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.188
or to to the surface

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:11.891
so that it could be tracked.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.893
A signal would be coming out off of that.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.762
The Coast Guard, the Canadians,

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.964
the bridge would be able to pick up

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:20.733
and then be able to start to track

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.068
where it might have come from.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:22.969
We'd be looking at

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:23.803
what has happened

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.573
in the last 48 hours to the weather

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.275
what conditions may have changed

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.710
that are not normal.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.678
What would have happened

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.079
with the currents

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.080
at the depths

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.480
and in

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.483
between the bottom at 12,000 plus feet

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.619
and the surface could occur

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.255
and have suddenly taken in over

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:43.856
overrode

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.092
the power of the unit submersible.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.562
That's down next would be that a proper

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.532
submersible should have a beacon or two

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.434
that would be attached to it.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:55.501
They could be sending out

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.503
an underwater signal

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.872
that would tell people how to find it.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:01.474
So they'll be

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.809
looking for those

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.978
looking at the weather and tracking on

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.813
what would have happened to

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.449
if it got taken off of the site.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:10.750
The Coast Guard

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.884
will certainly be doing

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.219
something very similar

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.188
and they'll be coming in with

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.656
their own trackers

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.890
if they find this beacon

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.360
that was released from the submersible,

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.961
they would see where it was tracked

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.830
the whether put

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.498
another one of their own in the water

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.232
and track it

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.367
and see how it would go

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.336
and where the possibilities would be.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.204
I know that

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.072
listening to one of the admirals,

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.807
the Coast Guard is coming in

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.109
with their lower

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.310
end, shallower

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:40.113
water side scan sonar units at the moment

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:43.016
with larger, more capable

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.585
pieces of equipment behind it.

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:46.619
And using side

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.688
scan based on the debris field.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.290
You'd have to have

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:52.091
a beautiful

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:55.094
mapping sequence of the entire wreck.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.930
It could be a layover, if you will.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.898
We would be

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:01.301
laying one on top of the other

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.102
in order to see what's new,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.538
what is there that we didn't see before.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.241
The potential's

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:11.944
one that the unit has

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.047
not had the power to maintain

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:15.381
with the current.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:19.686
More likely, based on the original videos

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:22.055
and images of things that Bob Ballard did

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:23.856
with the Titanic

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.958
is that is maybe quite on something.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.595
And I mean, these are huge concerns,

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.664
which obviously

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:35.501
So we do appreciate your time as we have

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.303
so many unanswered questions

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.171
at this point and quite

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:38.838
frankly, are trying

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.473
to get some more details

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.775
about those who are engaged

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.977
in the rescue here. Butch Hendrick.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.813
Thank you very much

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.381
for taking the time with us

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:49.982
this afternoon. We do appreciate it.

